  "body": "The [delete algorithm](https://wicg.github.io/cookie-store/#delete-cookie-algorithm) says:\n> Let expires be the earliest representable date represented\n> Let value be the empty string.\n> Return the results of running [set a cookie](https://wicg.github.io/cookie-store/#set-a-cookie) with url, name, value, expires, domain, path, sameSite, and partitioned.\n\nBut the [set cookie](https://wicg.github.io/cookie-store/#set-a-cookie) steps say:\n> If name’s [length](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-length) is 0 and value’s [length](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-length) is 0, then return failure.\n\nThat would mean `cookieStore.delete(\"\")` should always rejects.\n\nThe [web platform tests](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/27583d5afd9beea3a7551f35470cf188de1d368c/testing/web-platform/tests/cookie-store/change_eventhandler_for_no_name_and_no_value.https.window.js#20,38) currently assume that set throws for empty name and value, but delete with empty name works.\n\nI think the spec needs to be updated to account for this corner case.",
